<title>USA: Long Island Savings Bank sells $300 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Long Island Savings Bank sells $300 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Long Island Savings Bank was priced on Tuesday, according to lead manager Salomon Brothers Inc.</p>
<p>BORROWER LONG ISLAND SAVINGS BANK</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	 COUPON 7.00 PCT   MATURITY 6/13/2002</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.788  FIRST PAY DATE 12/13/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA3  YIELD 7.051 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>S&amp;P BBB		SPREAD 63 BPS     CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>U.S. Corporate Bond Unit 212-859-1678</p>
</text>
